I really want to try this in English, but I definitely wouldn't understand any of it. Whoa!

288
00:17:03,390 --> 00:17:07,190
Orange juice and milk.

289
00:17:07,190 --> 00:17:12,610
Sunflower oil, like salad oil.

290
00:17:12,610 --> 00:17:19,690
Let's see how far I can get — serve the baked trout, and at the end give a rating like a regular customer would.

291
00:17:19,690 --> 00:17:21,690
W-w-who's that!?

292
00:17:21,690 --> 00:17:25,300
Hey? Who are you?

293
00:17:25,300 --> 00:17:28,970
Okay, uh, oven-baked...

294
00:17:28,970 --> 00:17:31,770
Alright, grab the trout!

295
00:17:31,770 --> 00:17:34,570
Where to?

296
00:17:34,570 --> 00:17:36,370
Ah!

297
00:17:36,370 --> 00:17:39,040
Trout, trout, trout!

298
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:43,060
Got the trout! Huh?

299
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:45,860
Got it!

300
00:17:45,860 --> 00:17:47,660
Placed it!

301
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:48,740
It didn't fall.

302
00:17:48,740 --> 00:17:50,140
Umm...

303
00:17:50,140 --> 00:17:52,020
Wait, is it already time to cook?

304
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:52,620
Huh?

305
00:17:52,620 --> 00:17:54,720
Can I start with seasoning? Already?

306
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:57,280
Can I season it already?

307
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:57,800
Huh?

308
00:17:57,800 --> 00:18:01,600
Season it first, then—

309
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:03,440
Oh, then bake it?

310
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:06,100
Black pepper.

311
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:07,380
Huh? Black pepper?

312
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:11,260
This would definitely be more fun in English, but...

313
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:13,320
I mean, my English skills—

314
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:15,700
I don't have the English ability,

315
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:17,920
I'd be terrible at it, so I'll pass.

316
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,500
Umm...

317
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:22,620
Clock...

318
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:22,980
Found it!

319
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:26,660
No idea.

320
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:28,940
You do this kind of thing first?

321
00:18:28,940 --> 00:18:30,760
5 grams

322
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:31,880
1

323
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:32,400
2

324
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:33,020
3

325
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:33,620
4

326
00:18:33,620 --> 00:18:34,300
5

327
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:37,080
Polka doesn't know how to cook

328
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:42,070
Grab the spice container

329
00:18:42,070 --> 00:18:46,050
Did I even buy dill or anything like that?

330
00:18:46,050 --> 00:18:48,230
Thyme... oh, there's dill!

331
00:18:48,230 --> 00:18:56,270
Whoa whoa whoa, oh!

332
00:18:56,270 --> 00:19:00,380
How many dill do I need again? Huh?

333
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:05,380
5, right? But is it below?

334
00:19:12,390 --> 00:19:14,870
Oh, got it! I just need it checked off below

335
00:19:14,870 --> 00:19:16,430
So that means I don't have enough black pepper either?

336
00:19:16,430 --> 00:19:18,230
Oh, different!

337
00:19:18,230 --> 00:19:20,030
Oh!

338
00:19:20,030 --> 00:19:21,010
Oh!

339
00:19:21,010 --> 00:19:21,830
That's enough. Okay.

340
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:23,540
Nice.

341
00:19:23,540 --> 00:19:26,230
And thyme?

342
00:19:26,230 --> 00:19:28,830
Thyme. No.

343
00:19:28,830 --> 00:19:34,490
Alright, OK. Looking good.

344
00:19:34,490 --> 00:19:39,490
Now, the oven. Oven, oven, oven. Switch to the oven and bake!

345
00:19:39,490 --> 00:19:45,380
Oh, a wire rack was placed.

346
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:47,120
I can put it on the bottom or top

347
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:47,860
Let's go with the top

348
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:49,060
Bumped into it

349
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:52,520
When Polka was little

350
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:54,620
When I was little

351
00:19:54,620 --> 00:19:57,060
I opened a door and it hit me

352
00:19:57,060 --> 00:19:58,740
and I had to get stitches on my head. Want to hear that story?

353
00:19:58,740 --> 00:20:00,620
90 seconds

354
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:03,260
In the meantime, cut the lemon into quarters

355
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:06,510
Limon

356
00:20:06,510 --> 00:20:10,170
"Limon"...

357
00:20:10,170 --> 00:20:11,150
Come on

358
00:20:11,150 --> 00:20:14,290
Is it okay to just leave it there?

359
00:20:14,430 --> 00:20:16,430
Cut into 4 pieces and...

360
00:20:16,430 --> 00:20:18,230
Hm? Where did I put it?

361
00:20:18,230 --> 00:20:23,990
Here's the big problem!

362
00:20:23,990 --> 00:20:25,590
Hm? It ended on me...

363
00:20:25,590 --> 00:20:27,570
This cut is super hard!

364
00:20:27,570 --> 00:20:29,190
Umm...

365
00:20:29,190 --> 00:20:30,790
Here?

366
00:20:30,790 --> 00:20:32,790
1... nice!

367
00:20:32,790 --> 00:20:34,590
Oh, isn't this going pretty well?

368
00:20:34,590 --> 00:20:42,900
Alright!

369
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:46,030
Huh?

370
00:20:46,030 --> 00:20:48,030
Yes! Okay okay okay!

371
00:20:48,030 --> 00:20:50,030
Nice!

372
00:20:50,030 --> 00:20:52,430
Okay

373
00:20:52,430 --> 00:20:54,750
Done!

374
00:20:54,750 --> 00:20:57,460
And

375
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:59,480
I'm not really taking this seriously but somehow

376
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:01,280
Wait, this doesn't look serious

377
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:03,080
But seriously

378
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:04,160
it's coming together

379
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:05,180
Where did it go

380
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:08,060
It's actually coming together really well

381
00:21:08,060 --> 00:21:10,570
There we go, done

382
00:21:10,570 --> 00:21:11,430
OK

383
00:21:11,430 --> 00:21:20,370
It's not cooked

384
00:21:20,370 --> 00:21:23,360
It wasn't cooked

385
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:25,780
I thought I heard a ding

386
00:21:25,780 --> 00:21:26,540
Hmm

387
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:31,890
Wait, this is right, isn't it?

388
00:21:37,130 --> 00:21:40,280
Huh

389
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:43,400
90 seconds

390
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:43,980
Hm

391
00:21:43,980 --> 00:21:51,820
Do I have to set it to 90 seconds manually?

392
00:21:51,820 --> 00:21:54,360
Settings

393
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:57,130
Umm

394
00:21:57,130 --> 00:22:01,230
Where's the 90 seconds option?

395
00:22:01,230 --> 00:22:04,830
Something's off

396
00:22:13,270 --> 00:22:15,350
That's probably 9 minutes

397
00:22:16,370 --> 00:22:19,860
So 90 seconds is

398
00:22:19,860 --> 00:22:21,560
1.5

399
00:22:21,560 --> 00:22:25,680
Okay

400
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:34,620
Alright

401
00:22:34,620 --> 00:22:35,710
Buy a plate?

402
00:22:35,710 --> 00:22:37,270
Oh, but it's already done!

403
00:22:37,270 --> 00:22:37,590
Why?

404
00:22:37,590 --> 00:22:39,110
It's done!

405
00:22:39,110 --> 00:22:39,930
No way?

406
00:22:39,930 --> 00:22:45,940
How?

407
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:50,590
Oh, I ran out of money.

408
00:22:50,590 --> 00:22:54,270
And then, open here.

409
00:22:54,270 --> 00:22:54,790
Over there, over there!

410
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:56,170
Over there — I'm doing this with my bare hands, huh.

411
00:22:56,170 --> 00:22:58,170
The lemon got all browned.

412
00:22:58,170 --> 00:22:59,170
It turned out like a potato!

413
00:22:59,170 --> 00:23:00,170
What do I do?

414
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:01,970
It turned out like a potato, but is that okay?

415
00:23:01,970 --> 00:23:02,970
Is this fine?

416
00:23:02,970 --> 00:23:03,770
Is this the end?

417
00:23:03,770 --> 00:23:04,570
Seasoning, seasoning!

418
00:23:04,570 --> 00:23:05,570
Wait, I did that last.

419
00:23:05,570 --> 00:23:06,570
What was that again?

420
00:23:06,570 --> 00:23:07,570
What's there?

421
00:23:07,570 --> 00:23:08,370
Umm...

422
00:23:08,370 --> 00:23:09,370
What?

423
00:23:09,370 --> 00:23:10,370
Something's off.

424
00:23:10,370 --> 00:23:11,370
What, what, what?

425
00:23:11,370 --> 00:23:12,170
Over here...

426
00:23:12,170 --> 00:23:13,170
It's definitely not here.

427
00:23:13,170 --> 00:23:14,170
There!

428
00:23:14,170 --> 00:23:15,170
Safe and sound.

429
00:23:15,170 --> 00:23:16,170
Next to the long one.

430
00:23:16,170 --> 00:23:17,170
Umm...

431
00:23:17,170 --> 00:23:18,170
Floral Fresh?

432
00:23:18,170 --> 00:23:19,170
Hmm?

433
00:23:19,170 --> 00:23:23,330
Dodododododo!

434
00:23:23,330 --> 00:23:25,130
Whoa whoa whoa!

435
00:23:25,130 --> 00:23:30,930
Nice! Okay, this should do it!

436
00:23:30,930 --> 00:23:34,530
There are only three.

437
00:23:43,580 --> 00:23:44,880
Where did the other one go?

438
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:45,340
Huh?

439
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:49,750
The plate I'm holding.

440
00:23:49,750 --> 00:23:52,510
It went into the basic.

441
00:23:52,510 --> 00:23:53,470
Four!

442
00:23:53,470 --> 00:23:57,090
Where did this one fall?

443
00:23:57,090 --> 00:24:00,700
Huh?

444
00:24:00,700 --> 00:24:02,660
Shut up!

445
00:24:02,660 --> 00:24:03,280
That's me!

446
00:24:03,280 --> 00:24:05,180
Sorry!

447
00:24:05,180 --> 00:24:08,070
Umm...

448
00:24:08,070 --> 00:24:09,850
Lemon.

449
00:24:09,850 --> 00:24:11,130
Lemon.

450
00:24:11,130 --> 00:24:20,680
Whoa! Fleur? Fleur? Where is it? Let me buy a lemon!

451
00:24:21,350 --> 00:24:25,350
I followed the tutorial! Wait... huh?

452
00:24:25,350 --> 00:24:31,350
Did I not do it? Could it be...

453
00:24:31,350 --> 00:24:41,350
Huh? This is the tutorial, right? I was being super serious about it... there it is! Okay... umm... oh.

454
00:24:42,850 --> 00:24:46,050
Placing it here... I can't place it...

455
00:24:46,050 --> 00:24:54,900
Where did the lemon go... an eternal mystery...

456
00:24:58,590 --> 00:25:01,610
The work just keeps piling up!

457
00:25:01,610 --> 00:25:05,370
Ah! A pinch from here? Parsley leaves!

458
00:25:05,370 --> 00:25:08,880
Fresh?

459
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:10,480
Huh? Three whole leaves!?

460
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:12,120
Do you really need that many?

461
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:13,960
Do you really need that many?

462
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:16,280
Okay! Moving along the workflow here!

463
00:25:16,280 --> 00:25:17,580
Okay! Right here!

464
00:25:17,580 --> 00:25:19,720
Order!

465
00:25:20,690 --> 00:25:24,870
Serving — salmon with lemon.

466
00:25:24,870 --> 00:25:25,730
Huh?

467
00:25:25,730 --> 00:25:27,990
Oh! But look!

468
00:25:27,990 --> 00:25:30,310
The taste is pretty good, just slightly lacking.

469
00:25:30,310 --> 00:25:34,630
Hmm, but it's pretty good for a first dish.

470
00:25:34,630 --> 00:25:39,530
The lemon was a bit, you know, hmm...

471
00:25:39,530 --> 00:25:41,310
No complaints though — look, it's perfect!

472
00:25:41,310 --> 00:25:47,130
See! See!

473
00:25:47,130 --> 00:25:48,390
It's perfect!

474
00:25:48,390 --> 00:25:54,510
Alright, let's wait until opening time.

475
00:25:54,510 --> 00:26:00,990
Day 1 done — OK, 1,772 yen!

476
00:26:00,990 --> 00:26:05,590
Whoa, there's a park skill or something?

477
00:26:05,590 --> 00:26:10,130
I just have to keep leveling up proficiency.

478
00:26:10,130 --> 00:26:13,870
Oh right, I didn't level up before the next day started.

479
00:26:13,870 --> 00:26:15,870
Huh? Can't I go back?

480
00:26:15,870 --> 00:26:17,790
Huh? Really?

481
00:26:17,790 --> 00:26:22,100
Yes.

482
00:26:22,100 --> 00:26:24,910
So?

483
00:26:24,910 --> 00:26:30,100
Oh, hello! Are you excited too?

484
00:26:30,100 --> 00:26:33,880
Let's start serving today and make this restaurant the best in town!

485
00:26:33,880 --> 00:26:37,780
This is the prep phase. No explanation needed, I guess — no orders yet.

486
00:26:37,780 --> 00:26:38,860
That was fast.

487
00:26:38,860 --> 00:26:40,840
Oh, a plate? A plate is fine. A plate.

488
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:44,260
I just said it, so not that one — a plate.

489
00:26:44,260 --> 00:26:45,020
Huh? What?

490
00:26:45,810 --> 00:26:48,040
A laptop? A computer, out of nowhere?

491
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:50,580
Well, I guess you'd do this before opening.

492
00:26:50,580 --> 00:26:51,700
Umm...

493
00:26:51,700 --> 00:26:54,680
Skills? A skill upgrade — I can get one!

494
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:56,000
There it is! Level up!

495
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:58,740
Okay, okay, okay! Level up, level up!

496
00:26:58,740 --> 00:27:00,480
Alright!

497
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:01,680
And...

498
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:04,200
What I currently have is...

499
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:06,060
Oh, it's explaining the skills.

500
00:27:06,060 --> 00:27:08,140
Whoa, so that was actually really important.

501
00:27:08,140 --> 00:27:09,060
Oh, sorry!

502
00:27:09,060 --> 00:27:10,480
Perks.

503
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:11,100
Okay.

504
00:27:11,100 --> 00:27:15,220
Wow, the gameplay just got a lot deeper.

505
00:27:15,220 --> 00:27:18,210
Alright!

506
00:27:18,210 --> 00:27:20,740
Laptop.

507
00:27:20,740 --> 00:27:23,800
Wait, wait — important stuff, slow down a little.

508
00:27:23,800 --> 00:27:24,540
Huh?

509
00:27:24,540 --> 00:27:27,860
Huh?

510
00:27:27,860 --> 00:27:30,040
You were saying something important, weren't you?

511
00:27:30,040 --> 00:27:31,780
Whoa, suddenly—

512
00:27:31,780 --> 00:27:36,750
There it is.

513
00:27:36,750 --> 00:27:37,990
To help with—

514
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:38,470
Who's that?

515
00:27:38,470 --> 00:27:41,370
Today's first order is boiled—

516
00:27:41,370 --> 00:27:44,070
We're boiling potatoes, so find me a large pot.

517
00:27:44,070 --> 00:27:44,830
A pot!

518
00:27:44,830 --> 00:27:47,850
I'm actually a little happy the tutorial is finally showing up.

519
00:27:47,850 --> 00:27:51,690
It says about 1 liter, so I guess being a little off is fine.

520
00:27:51,690 --> 00:27:51,830
Hmm?

521
00:27:51,830 --> 00:27:54,830
Done! Done!

522
00:27:54,830 --> 00:27:57,090
Hmm? 1 liter — how many liters is that?

523
00:27:57,090 --> 00:27:58,750
1000.

524
00:27:58,750 --> 00:28:02,450
Huh? Huh? Huh?

525
00:28:02,450 --> 00:28:05,700
This...

526
00:28:05,700 --> 00:28:07,440
Done! Done!

527
00:28:07,440 --> 00:28:08,260
Wait, oh—

528
00:28:08,260 --> 00:28:09,580
So?

529
00:28:09,580 --> 00:28:11,780
Umm...

530
00:28:11,780 --> 00:28:15,400
Add salt to the large pot.

531
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:16,980
Even if you eavesdrop on that—

532
00:28:16,980 --> 00:28:18,040
Umm...

533
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:18,760
Salt.

534
00:28:18,760 --> 00:28:20,660
Into the large pot.

535
00:28:20,660 --> 00:28:22,040
Salt.

536
00:28:22,040 --> 00:28:23,500
20.

537
00:28:23,500 --> 00:28:29,520
Okay!

538
00:28:29,520 --> 00:28:30,580
Alright!

539
00:28:30,580 --> 00:28:33,460
Into the pot—

540
00:28:33,460 --> 00:28:37,500
While holding the pot—

541
00:28:37,500 --> 00:28:37,920
Potatoes.

542
00:28:37,920 --> 00:28:38,300
Oh, wait a sec.

543
00:28:38,300 --> 00:28:40,320
So it's better to put them in while holding the pot.

544
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:41,320
There we go.

545
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:45,090
Pota—

546
00:28:45,090 --> 00:28:46,570
That works.

547
00:28:46,570 --> 00:28:46,850
Found them!

548
00:28:46,850 --> 00:28:49,950
It keeps going down and down.

549
00:28:49,950 --> 00:28:52,250
Is this okay?

550
00:28:52,250 --> 00:28:55,670
Understood.

551
00:28:55,670 --> 00:28:59,230
It still feels like I'm being taught everything.

552
00:28:59,230 --> 00:28:59,870
Yes.

553
00:28:59,870 --> 00:29:01,150
Subke—

554
00:29:01,150 --> 00:29:04,310
Lamy's favorite—

555
00:29:04,310 --> 00:29:07,900
Here.

556
00:29:07,900 --> 00:29:11,280
Black salt.

557
00:29:11,280 --> 00:29:12,520
Black pepper.

558
00:29:12,520 --> 00:29:14,500
With salt and black pepper—

559
00:29:14,500 --> 00:29:17,280
Seasoning.

560
00:29:17,280 --> 00:29:25,010
Is that okay?

561
00:29:25,010 --> 00:29:28,260
Alright, looks good!

562
00:29:35,570 --> 00:29:36,180
Okay!

563
00:29:36,180 --> 00:29:39,480
Grab a pot.

564
00:29:39,480 --> 00:29:39,900
Hm?

565
00:29:39,900 --> 00:29:43,440
This one?

566
00:29:43,440 --> 00:29:47,250
No wait, this is a big pot.

567
00:29:47,250 --> 00:29:48,770
And it's on the wrong side!

568
00:29:48,770 --> 00:29:51,710
Hey!

569
00:29:51,710 --> 00:29:55,310
Whaaat? Whaaat? Whaaat?

